# Accessibility

Inclusive UI is a standing product constraint. Do not treat it as optional polish or defer it to a later cleanup when changing panes, navigation, forms, or dynamic status UI.

A fuller accessibility pass is chartered in GitHub [#161](https://github.com/dustinestes/Hatchery/issues/161). Until that work is scheduled, **do not regress** keyboard use, labeling, focus, or color-only status.

## Defaults

- Prefer **visible text labels**; collapsed icon rails are opt-in density, not the primary IA
- Every icon-only control needs an accessible name (`aria-label` and/or `title`)
- Primary flows must work **keyboard-only** with a **visible focus** ring/state
- Custom widgets (sidebar flyouts, notification tray, password toggles, dialogs) support Escape / Enter consistently with existing patterns
- Status and alerts must not rely on **color alone** — keep text (or another non-color cue)
- Live regions (toasts, trays, event feeds) get appropriate roles/labels; don’t leave updates announce-hostile
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` when adding motion

## When adding UI

```
✅ Labeled nav item + keyboard path + focus style
✅ Badge with text (“Provisioning”) not color-only meaning
✅ Flyout reachable when the sidebar is collapsed (not hover-only with no name)

❌ Pointer-only control with no keyboard equivalent
❌ Icon button with no accessible name
❌ “We’ll fix a11y in the v2 pass” for a regression you introduced
```

Human-facing guidance: [`CONTRIBUTING.md` — Accessibility](../../CONTRIBUTING.md#accessibility).
